 - Bash: S=<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/ours-src/bin/<tool>; node $S --group-by ext --merge-identities; echo ----; node $S --group-by ext
 - Bash: cd <home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/f9/claude-opus-5-5/P/runs/E3-ours-1/repo; for c in 62628c0 739dc11 fcd2b56 00d6eec; do git show --stat --format='%h %an %s' $c | tail -n +1 | head -8; echo; done
FINAL ANSWER:
Each file type has a different top owner. I counted surviving lines with `git blame -w -M -C` at HEAD across all 18 files: 1,662 non-blank lines were attributed, 1,995 counting blank lines.

| Ext | Lines | Top owner | Runner-up | Bus factor (50%) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` (7 files) | 1,032 | **Troy Goode, 564 (54.7%)** merged. Unmerged: <email redacted> 520 (50.4%) + troy@laptop.example 44 (4.3%) | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 362 (35.1%) | 1 |
| `.yml` (6) | 314 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson, 101 (32.2%)** | Íñigo Marquínez Prado, 80 (25.5%) | 2 |
| `.md` (2) | 253 | **Troy Goode, 71 (28.1%)** | Jon Church, 59 (23.3%) | 2 |
| `.json` (1) | 40 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson, 20 (50.0%)** | Troy Goode, 12 (30.0%) | 1 |
| no extension (2) | 23 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson, 21 (91.3%)** | Troy Goode, 2 (8.7%) | 1 |

Only `.js`, `.json` and the files without an extension have one person holding at least half the lines. `.yml` and `.md` don't.

**Bus factor** here means the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50% of that file type's lines. I computed it per file type, at the 50% threshold only. I did not run the 80% variant.

**Duplicate identities (guesses from names and addresses, not confirmed):**
- **Troy Goode** shows up under <email redacted> (93 commits) and troy@laptop.example (2 commits). The evidence is strong (same name), so the `.js` row leads with the merged figure. Nothing is written to `.mailmap`. To make it permanent, run `--identities` and add the line it prints, after you confirm it is one person.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** and **alex94puchades** use the same address, so the tool counts them as one person. Their row in `.js` is 30 lines (2.9%). The `.mailmap` line would be:
  `Alejandro Caravaca Puchades <<email redacted>> alex94puchades <<email redacted>>`

**Left out or adjusted:**
- **Reformat commit 62628c0** ("style: reformat js…", by Fiona Formatter) is ignored. It rewrote 1,016 lines in 4 files (`lib/index.js` and three test files) and changed only indentation and quotes. If it were counted, it would hold 291 lines, mostly taken from Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson.
- **dependabot[bot]** is excluded (10 lines, 11 commits).

**Mechanical rewrite check:** the tool examined 136 commits and set aside only 62628c0. It flagged 5 more as possibly mechanical and kept all of them:
- 739dc11 (license reformat, 17 lines)
- fcd2b56 (ESLint switch mixed with cleanup, 11 lines)
- 00d6eec (eslint config moved to YAML, 9 lines)
- 344ce1e and 9c2b59d (1 line each)

They are small, and fcd2b56 includes real code changes, so the shares above count them.

These numbers show whose lines still exist. They don't measure code quality, review work, or deleted code.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | awk -F/ '{f=$NF; if (f ~ /\./ && f !~ /^\.[^.]*$/) {sub(/.*\./,"",f); print f} else print "(none)"}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; git log --format='%h %an <%ae> %s' -8; git show --stat 62628c0 | tail -5; git show --stat b2005d9 | tail -3; git show --stat 02afce3 | tail -3
 - Bash: ls -a .mailmap .git-blame-ignore-revs 2>&1; git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -30
run() { for f in $(git ls-files); do b=$(basename "$f"); case "$b" in *.*) e="${b##*.}"; [ "$b" = ".$e" ] && e="(none)";; *) e="(none)";; esac
  git blame --line-porcelain $@ -- "$f" | sed -n 's/^author-mail //p' | sed "s|^|$e |"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr; }
echo "== RAW"; run; echo "== IGNORE 62628c0"; run --ignore-rev 62628c0
FINAL ANSWER:
Blame on HEAD (`master`, 62628c0), counted by author email:

| Ext | Files | Top owner (surviving lines) | Runner-up |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 7 | **Fiona Formatter**: 1016 / 1202 (85%) | Troy Goode: 139 (two emails combined) |
| `.yml` | 6 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**: 117 / 383 | Íñigo Marquínez Prado: 94 |
| `.md` | 2 | **Troy Goode**: 104 / 345 | Jon Church: 72 |
| `.json` | 1 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**: 20 / 42 | Troy Goode: 12 |
| no extension | 2 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**: 21 / 27 | Troy Goode: 6 |

**The `.js` result is misleading.** Fiona owns those lines because of one commit, 62628c0 "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes". It changed 1016 lines across `lib/index.js` and three test files and did not change behavior. When I re-ran blame with `--ignore-rev 62628c0`:

| `.js` owner | Lines |
|---|---|
| **Troy Goode** | 520 (473 from <email redacted> + 47 from troy@laptop.example) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 339 |
| Fiona Formatter | 237 (lines git couldn't trace back past the reformat, mostly quote-style changes) |
| Others | 106 |

For "who wrote the JS code", the answer is **Troy Goode**. The other file types are the same with or without ignoring the reformat.

The repo has no `.mailmap`, so identities are matched by email only. I treated `troy@laptop.example` (author of the two newest commits besides the reformat) as the same person as `<email redacted>` because the name matches. That doesn't change any winner.

If you want blame to skip the reformat by default, you could add 62628c0 to a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file.
